    kg:textSpan "We found some recent inference optimization works that argue against persistent context selection ( Tang et al. , 2024 ). However, all of these texts show that heavy hitters do not persist when using a tiny cache budget (<5%). We empirically verify persistent context selection by measuring the fraction of heavy hitters that persist during the entire generation phase of H 2 O when using a large cache budget. We observe that nearly 60-80% of the heavy hitters selected during the prefill stage pers" .

