    kg:textSpan "investigation, we found that BitsandBytes adopted the dual-kernel method (discussed in Section 4.1 ) to support FP4 quantization. During the execution of the first kernel, the FP4 model weights will be first loaded from global memory, de-quantized into FP16, and then written back to global memory in the FP16 data type. After that, a normal 7 Evaluation We evaluate the performance at two levels: kernel-level benchmarking using TC-FPx GPU kernels and model-level end-toend inference using DeepSpeed" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/2401_14112_rag__chunk_018> a kg:Chunk ;
