    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2401_14112_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "FP6-LLM can at most set the inference batch size to 16 before running out of GPU memory while the FP16 baseline can at most serve 4 requests in a batch. As a result, FP6-LLM can at most achieve 319.1 tokens per GPU-second ( 4 . 05 higher) with batch size 16 while the FP16 baseline can at most achieve 78.8 tokens per GPU-second with batch size 4, given the same GPU budget. Besides, FP6-LLM can achieve 1 . 91 / 1 . 84 / 1 . 72 higher generation throughput compared to the FP16 baseline when their b" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/2401_14351_rag__chunk_000> a kg:Chunk ;
