    kg:docId "2401.14351_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2401_14351_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "the inference duration ( d ) and the average time to produce a token ( t ), we calculate t out = d / t . For selecting the optimal server for model migration, ServerlessLLM employs a dynamic programming approach to minimize migration time. manager, (ii) examining the efficiency and overheads associated with live migration for LLM inference, and (iii) evaluating ServerlessLLM against a large-scale serverless workload, modelled on real-world serverless trace data. 7.1 Evaluation Setup Setup. We ha" .

