    kg:textSpan "teachers. We demonstrate that leveraging complementary teachers benefits the distillation quality. Also, D IVERSE D ISTILL significantly increases distillation performance when dealing with a diverse teacher committee, leading to the best student compared to various baselines across different teacher choices. 2 Related Work 2.1 Foundation Model for Specific Application Foundation models are trained on massive amounts of data and can be applied across various downstream tasks. Example models incl" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/2402_14808_rag__chunk_004> a kg:Chunk ;
    kg:chunkId "2402.14808_rag::chunk_004" ;
    kg:docId "2402.14808_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2402_14808_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "The acceleration of our approach comes from reducing redundant memory access of the KV cache. Therefore, it is orthogonal and complementary to prefix sharing in PagedAttention ( Kwon et al. , 2023 ), which eliminates redundant memory footprint of system prompts, and is unlike PromptCache ( Gim et al. , 2023 ), which eliminates the redundant computation of the reusable prefix KVs and thus only acceler- 3 Methodology In this section, we elaborate on the proposed approach. We begin with a brief pre" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/2402_15678_rag__chunk_002> a kg:Chunk ;
    kg:chunkId "2402.15678_rag::chunk_002" ;
    kg:docId "2402.15678_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2402_15678_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "certain scenarios. In addition, these methods typically require fine-tuning the LLM to reach the desired accuracy, which is hardly affordable economically for the majority of researchers and practitioners. Speculative decoding [ 3 , 19 , 25 ], as an emerging technique to accelerate LLM inference, harnesses a small speculative model (SSM) to expedite the inference process of LLM. Advantageously, it requires no modifications to the LLM itself and thus does not require additional retraining or fine" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/2402_15678_rag__chunk_003> a kg:Chunk ;
    kg:chunkId "2402.15678_rag::chunk_003" ;
    kg:docId "2402.15678_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2402_15678_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "optimal setting of speculation length? Finally, the existing methods tightly couple the execution of SSM and LLM, which introduces significant idle time during the interaction of SSM decoding and LLM verification. For example, the sequential execution of SSM decoding and LLM verification forces either SSM or LLM to stay idle when the other is working in progress. Challenge 3: How to effectively decouple the execution of SSM and LLM in order to reduce the idle time during decoding and verificatio" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/2402_15678_rag__chunk_006> a kg:Chunk ;
    kg:chunkId "2402.15678_rag::chunk_006" ;
    kg:docId "2402.15678_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2402_15678_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "exhibits a decreasing-then-increasing trend when increasing the speculation length of SSM. An optimal setting of speculation length exists that minimizes the LLM inference time. The reason is that a larger speculation length can reduce the number of LLM verifications, which effectively improves the performance of speculation decoding. However, when the speculation length reaches a turning point (asterisk in Figure 2 ), the computation cost of LLM verification rises significantly, which offsets t" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/2402_15678_rag__chunk_012> a kg:Chunk ;
    kg:chunkId "2402.15678_rag::chunk_012" ;
    kg:docId "2402.15678_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2402_15678_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "verification. Hence, the execution of SSMs is not constrained by LLM. And as long as there are available requests in the intermediate resulting pool , LLM can sustain continuous execution. To ensure efficient execution of the pipeline, a crucial consideration is the speed of SSM speculation. Avoiding bubbles in the LLM execution process is a key factor in achieving a high throughput pipeline mechanism. Fortunately, due to the large discrepancy in parameter scale between SSM and LLM, the executio" .

