    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2402_15678_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "LLM Batch 3 (B3) ... SSM Batch 4 (B4) B4 ... B1 B3 B2 B2 B1 B3 B2 Intermediate Resulting Pool Figure 7: The workflow of the speculative generation pipeline and the status of the intermediate resulting pool in the absence of any control. T i denotes the duration during which requests from Batch i are queued in the intermediate resulting pool . sufficient quantity of requests before the completion of LLM verification, thereby satisfying the imposed constraint. 4 Implementation We have implemented " .

