    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2402_16363_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "during inference. For example, the inputs of each transformer layer are kept in memory until the residual addition is executed. (3) for auto-regressive LLMs, caching key and value activations (KV cache) into memory is necessary for subsequent token generation. We utilize LLM-Viewer to analyze the effects of quantization on these tensors from three perspectives: computation, memory consumption, and memory access. Computation : The latest computing devices, such as NVIDIA GPUs, generally support F" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/2402_16363_rag__chunk_009> a kg:Chunk ;
