    kg:textSpan "Tmp Act 0.8 0.6 0.4 Memory Access : Quantizing tensors in LLM can significantly reduce memory access, resulting in fewer data bytes to be moved for the same amount of computation. This increase in arithmetic intensity contributes to the Roofline model, leading to three scenarios: (1) After quantization, the arithmetic intensity remains within the memory-bound range. With the improvement in arithmetic intensity, the average data access per computation is reduced, alleviating the pressure on data " .

