    kg:docId "2407.11798_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2407_11798_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "generating speculative trees whenever the head node would otherwise be idle. The idle state is determined by probing for an incoming logits transfer transaction. If a transaction is waiting to be processed, the head node invokes the sampling and verification routine. Otherwise, the node generates another speculation tree. By opportunistically generating speculations, system utilization improves proportionally to the pipeline depth. A timeline of continuous speculation is shown in Figure 3. Specu" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/2407_12391_rag__chunk_004> a kg:Chunk ;
