    kg:textSpan "23 ]) eliminates inter-task resource interference by statically partitioning the GPUs compute units and VRAM channels at the software level (3.2). Our characterization with realistic workloads (3.1) indicates that these approaches cannot achieve both low latency for LS services and high throughput for BE tasks when they are colocated . Although hardware partitioning (FGPU [ 23 ]) isolates SMs and VRAM channels, it remains impractical for most GPUs (including newer models) due to its strong assum" .

