    kg:textSpan "BE tasks decreases as the concurrency of LS services increases (Fig. 5a). This is because Orion imposes numerous constraints on the co-execution of BE kernels to ensure low latency for LS tasks, as it cannot avoid intra-SM and inter-SM interference. These constraints limit the BE task throughput. For the BE models listed in Tab. 3, 73.8% of their kernels are subjected to at least one constraint (Fig. 5b). These excessive constraints lead to decreased BE task throughput as the load of the LS serv" .

