    kg:textSpan "can fully utilize the VRAM bandwidth by moving all memory-bound tensors to the reserved memory pool mapped to all VRAM channels. To achieve fast VRAM bandwidth scaling, for each memory-bound BE tensor, SGDRC maintains its 2 copies : 1) one mapped to all VRAM channels; and 2) one mapped to of the VRAM channels. For each memory-bound BE kernel, SGDRC passes its parameters based on two cases (Fig. 14): a) Monopolization state (when the LS kernel queue is empty): All input weight tensors and output " .

