    kg:textSpan "latency spikes lasting for 100s of seconds whenever long requests block the system. These spikes occur because arriving short requests must wait for the entire prefill computation of the long request to complete which can take several minutes. The convoy effect is a well-studied problem in operating systems with a known solution: preemptive scheduling. Chunked prefills [ 6 ] provide a natural mechanism for preemptable prefill computation. However, applying preemption to LLM inference faces three" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/2409_17264_rag__chunk_018> a kg:Chunk ;
