    kg:textSpan "these metrics used to evaluate the performance of LLM serving can be divided into two main groups: Service Level Objectives (SLOs, in Section 3) are the metrics that directly represent the token delivery state of a request. These include response time metrics such as TTFT, TBT, and TPOT, which help assess whether the request can deliver responses within the expected time frame. By defining SLOs, providers establish observable thresholds to proactively assess compliance with user expectations, wh" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/2410_14257_rag__chunk_009> a kg:Chunk ;
