    kg:textSpan "dispatch for execution, and how to batch requests. Typically, scheduling decisions are made at two levels (Figure 1 ). First, a request hits a load balancer that decides which server a request should be routed to. Here, each server holds a replica of the LLM which allows 1 Introduction Large Language Models (LLMs) are capable of powerful text generations that power chat bots, code assistants, and more. For a given request, the LLM predicts the next response token by conditioning on previous toke" .

