    kg:textSpan "few tokens left to be generated (as estimated by the predictor). A running request may be preempted in favour of a newly-arrived request, if the new request is estimated to have fewer remaining tokens than the running request. To avoid unnecessary preemption overheads, TRAIL defines a parameter 0 c 1 and only allows requests to be preempted in the beginning, when num _ generated _ tokens / est _ response _ length < c . TRAIL is not a drop-in replacement to current schedulers as it uses the layer" .

