    kg:docId "2412.03131_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2412_03131_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "the significance of other tokens when constructing its contextualized representation. During autoregressive inference, the attention mechanism operates in a causal manner, attending only to preceding tokens. Mathematically, the standard attention computation is defined as: s . During inference, the original tensor is approximately reconstructed via dequantization: X = s Q + z . Unlike the quantized tensor Q , the metadata s and z are kept in higher precision (e.g., FP16) to ensure more accurate " .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/2412_03131_rag__chunk_011> a kg:Chunk ;
