    kg:textSpan "[ 88 ] introduced a more flexible decoder-only architecture. It showed that encoders are rigid, non-current structures that fix output lengths, whereas decoder-only architectures use recurrent structures that leverage previously generated tokens to generate outputs of arbitrary length. Most modern LLMs now follow this decoderonly structure, stacking hundreds of identical layers to extract features (Figure 2). Despite their size, the number of unique architecture components in these LLMs is small" .

