    kg:textSpan "the TE-Pre-load step still remains the dominant factor in scaling time, although this latency can be further reduced through pre-warming ( 6.1 ). 6.2 Optimizing Model Loading D EEP S ERVE has two model-loading paths: local loading via PCIe from local DRAM or SSD, and NPU-fork using highspeed NPU-to-NPU links from a running TE. While NPUfork is generally faster, it has higher hardware requirements and cannot be used during code start (scaling from 0 TE). Local loading with pre-warming. We use the" .

