    kg:textSpan "global batch. This repeated execution degrades inference performance, as model weight matrices must be loaded from global memory repeatedly. This inefficiency is especially significant in the decode stage, where weight-loading overhead accounts for a substantial portion of total execution time. As a result, pipeline parallelism generally underperforms relative to tensor parallelism in the decode stage due to the amplified weight loading overhead. Decode (4 GPUs) Decode (8 GPUs) Figure 4. An exam" .

