    kg:docId "2504.09590_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2504_09590_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "the system from Poisson distribution with different request rates. Compared to the FCFS policy, preemptive scheduling effectively reduces normalized latency (Fig. 3a) by minimizing the overall queuing time (Fig. 3b) for waiting requests in the system. Challenges. However, existing iterative preemption approaches face a scheduling dilemma to balance TTFT and TPOT SLOs for RT requests. For example, vLLM preempts decode RT requests for incoming prefill requests, which sacrifices the high context ra" .

