    kg:textSpan "T IME ( req ) 5 req . goodput E STIMATE G OODPUT ( req ) 6 req . priority req . goodput requests. For latency-sensitive requests, explicit SLOs (e.g., TBT ) already define the per-token service bandwidth. Because maintaining a fixed bandwidth throughout a requests lifetime is impractical due to runtime dynamics (e.g., new request arrivals or early completions), GMAX amortizes bandwidth allocation over discrete scheduling frames of length . As illustrated in Figure 10 , execution is decomposed in" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/2504_20068_rag__chunk_014> a kg:Chunk ;
