    kg:docId "2504.20828_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2504_20828_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "[ 8 ] prioritizes prefill to reduce TTFT, at the cost of increased chance of generation stalls. More recently, Sarathi-Serve [ 1 ] introduced chunked prefill, which improves TBT by interleaving decoding with prefill but suffers from higher TTFT due to frequent I/O access. Another approach, DistServe [ 29 ], decouples prefill and decode by running them on separate GPUs. While simple, this disaggregation leads to resource underutilization prefill is compute-heavy but memory-light, and decode is co" .

