    kg:textSpan "Observation 2: LoRA introduces costly artifacts loading latency. Existing solutions [ 16 , 25 , 44 ] focus solely on loading the backbone checkpoint (from RAM, SSD, or remote storage) while neglecting the overhead of loading libraries, LoRA adapters, and just-in-time (JIT) compiled CUDA kernels. Observation 3: Serving multi-LoRA magnifies resource contention. LoRA-based applications often utilize diverse backbone models and adapters with varying mappings [ 27 , 48 ], necessitating the invocation" .

