    kg:textSpan "overall decoding time. Modern attention variants such as Grouped-Query Attention (GQA) [ 3 ], Multi-Query Attention (MQA) [ 4 ], and Multi-Head Latent Attention (MLA) [ 5 ] reduce KV-cache pressure by merging multiple keys and values into shared representations, i.e., collapsing Q original query heads into K KV heads where K < Q . A typical value of K is 8 or less in modern LLMs. For MLA, there is just a single latent representation of both K and V for all Q heads. Tensor Parallelism (TP) [ 6 ] " .

