    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2508_20274_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "Predictable LLM Serving on GPU Clusters Erfan Darzi Harvard University, MIT Cambridge, MA, USA Shreeanant Bharadwaj Northeastern University Boston, MA, USA Sree Bhargavi Balija University of California, San Diego La Jolla, CA, USA ABSTRACT tails persist above threshold, enforces dwell/cool-down to avoid thrashing, and returns resources when the system is stable. Our approach complements recent work showing the benefits of dynamic MIG reconfiguration [ 3 , 8 ] and PCIe-aware scheduling [ 7 ], but" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/2508_20274_rag__chunk_001> a kg:Chunk ;
    kg:chunkId "2508.20274_rag::chunk_001" ;
    kg:docId "2508.20274_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2508_20274_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "a bottleneck during intensive data transfers between the host and GPU [ 4 , 7 ]. Our scope includes LLM serving with vLLM; we additionally track time-to-first-token (TTFT) tails. This challenge is particularly acute in multi-tenant environments with limited visibility into the underlying hardware topology, including PCIe lane allocation and Non-Uniform Memory Access (NUMA) domains [ 2 ]. In practice, MIG provides hard isolation for compute and HBM but not for the shared PCIe path, so co-running " .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/2508_20274_rag__chunk_002> a kg:Chunk ;
    kg:chunkId "2508.20274_rag::chunk_002" ;
    kg:docId "2508.20274_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2508_20274_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "if insufficient do we enlarge the MIG slice. When relaxing isolation, we select a smaller profile whose placement score remains below a conservative threshold, preventing regressions. Streaming Multiprocessor (SM) and memory bandwidth utilization to identify compute or memory pressure, and host-level I/O statistics to correlate with storage-intensive noisy neighbors. Optionally, Network Interface Controller (NIC) and Interrupt Request (IRQ) statistics can be used to identify network or host-leve" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/2508_20274_rag__chunk_003> a kg:Chunk ;
    kg:chunkId "2508.20274_rag::chunk_003" ;
    kg:docId "2508.20274_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2508_20274_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "7 ]. Finally, the controller can apply lightweight, host-level Guardrails . These include adjusting the Multi-Process Service (MPS) active thread percentage to cap a tenants concurrency and applying cgroup I/O throttles using io.max to limit the disk bandwidth of a noisy background job [ 9 ]. 2.2.1 Topology-aware placement heuristic. We query GPU and PCIe topology via DCGM/NVML and host tools including lspci and NUMA maps to form a simple placement score for each candidate MIG instance. The scor" .

