    kg:docId "2511.02248_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2511_02248_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "model parameters but also activations and the keyvalue (KV) cache during generation. Therefore, memory profiling considers both weight memory and activation memory. Weight memory corresponds to the static storage of model parameters, while activation memory refers to the intermediate tensors and KV cache generated during forward pass computation that depend on request sequence lengths. By monitoring operator memory usage under varying sequence lengths, we quantify each operators memory sensitivi" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/2511_04791_rag__chunk_001> a kg:Chunk ;
