    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2511_04791_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "usage. In contrast, improving resource utilization and throughput (measured in tokens/sec or requests/sec) benefits from larger batch sizes. Balancing this tradeoff is central to scaling online serving systems efficiently. The key hardware resources involved include the GPUs high-bandwidth memory (HBM) capacity, memory bandwidth, and streaming multiprocessors (SMs). LLM inference consists of two distinct phases with different resource requirements: (1) the prefill phase, which encodes the input " .

