    kg:docId "2511.14510_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2511_14510_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "and Motivation 2.1 LLM Inference and Top- Attention In large language models (LLMs), the attention module plays a role in capturing the semantic relationships between input tokens, which is crucial for language modeling. Generally, the attention module includes individual heads, which is also called multi-head attention (MHA)[ 41 ]. Given the input hidden states X R ( indicates sequence length and is the hidden dimension), each attention head first projects X 2 via head-specific weight matrices " .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/2511_14510_rag__chunk_006> a kg:Chunk ;
    kg:chunkId "2511.14510_rag::chunk_006" ;
    kg:docId "2511.14510_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2511_14510_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "optimizations, a performance gap remains compared with the ideal case with a sufficient large GPU HBM to store the full KVCache. As Figure 2 shows, the perlayer decoding latency of RetroInfer, InfiniGen, and PQCache rises to 137%, 337%, and 354% against the ideal, mainly due to three factors: Cache management involves the cache lookup and update operations detailed in Section 2.2, particularly the CPU-based linked list maintenance. Host data transfer involves transferring the required top- KV da" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/2511_21862_rag__chunk_001> a kg:Chunk ;
