    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2512_00719_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "when compute stages are balanced; by Littles law ( Little , 1961 ), the longer last stage inflates queueing and tail latency. In short, the causes of sampling cost do not shrink with faster GEMMs, so the epilogue becomes the new critical path. It is therefore time to re-architect sampling so it returns to an inconspicuous final step rather than an invisible performance hog. 2.1 LLM Inference We first outline the workflow of modern LLM inference: A pretrained model takes a textual prompt as input" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/2512_03416_rag__chunk_016> a kg:Chunk ;
