    kg:textSpan "for a realistic workload mix. 2) Adaptation to burst workload.: We analyze how TokenScale adapts to burst workloads. In this experiment, we start the system from 1 prefiller and 1 Convertible Decoder to serve a stable traffic of 1 request/sec. At timestamp t = 10 s , the RPS is scaled to 10 requests/sec to emulate a traffic burst. Fig. 10a shows that TokenScale experiences only a slight increase in TTFT, rising to approximately 50 ms, and quickly recovers at t = 14 s. In contrast, all other base" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/2512_03416_rag__chunk_017> a kg:Chunk ;
