    kg:textSpan "small limit leads to fewer requests being processed per iteration and lower throughput, whereas an excessively large limit causes resource contention and redundant recomputation. In this paper, we propose AugServe , an efficient inference serving framework designed to reduce request queuing latency and improve effective throughput for augmented LLM inference services. We introduce a two-stage adaptive request scheduling strategy (C1) , which adaptively makes scheduling decisions based on the fea" .

