    kg:textSpan "where the draft model is the same as the original one: Using greedy decoding, all output of the draft model will be accepted, therefore maximizing the efficiency. Conversely, rejection sampling introduces extra overhead, as the draft model and the original model are sampled independently. Even if their distributions align perfectly, the output of the draft model may still be rejected. Examining this scheme leads to several insights. Firstly, when the temperature is set to 0 , it reverts to greed" .

