    kg:textSpan "[ 11 ] and Bert-Large [ 9 ] that are sequence-to-sequence, LLMs generate tokens one by one in an inference process that comprises two phases [ 31 , 40 ](Fig. 2): prefill and decode [ 32 ]. In the prefill phase, the input prompt sequence produces key/value (KV) caches for each transformer layer, which is used in the attention mechanism as a context vector for later token generation. During 2 on V100, while the execution time ratio is 7.29 for the decode phase. Since the LLM inference time contain" .

