    kg:textSpan "the de facto standard for dynamic memory allocation in LLM serving systems, e.g., TensorRT-LLM, HuggingFace TGI, LightLLM [ 4 , 6 , 28 ] etc. However, we show that PagedAttention faces a fundamental consequence of dynamic memory allocation: dynamically allocated objects are not guaranteed to be contiguous . Note that user-level objects are allocated in virtual memory. Therefore, in trying to enable dynamic allocation of physical memory, PagedAttention ends up changing the virtual memory layout o" .

