    kg:textSpan "systems [ 1 , 8 , 29 ] process incoming requests in a First-Come, First-Served (FCFS) fashion. However, strict FCFS scheduling does not always align with the systems throughput or SLO objectives. For example, if the goal is to defer prefill computation until closer to its associated deadline (prefill SLO), then FCFS may schedule the request too early, resulting in inefficient GPU utilization. This motivates the adoption of out-of-order scheduling in the LP instance. While FCFS is traditionally u" .

