    kg:textSpan "current scheduling mechanisms. First, preemption is used solely as a passive memory management strategy, rather than as a proactive tool for optimizing resource allocation. Second, although excess token generation can create buffers that would allow non-disruptive request eviction, existing methods fail to take advantage of this opportunity. As a result, these systems struggle to adapt dynamically to real-time Text-streaming refers to a progressive token generation and delivery process in LLM de" .

