    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2502_12574_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "by Head-wise Offloading Attention with KV Cache. During the computation of self-attention at time step t , the model utilizes the entire sequence of keys and values from time steps 1 to t (stored in the KV cache) alongside the new query Q t : 2.2. Lossy KV Cache Management Evit KV cache can reduce memory usage and computational complexity. One direction is to identify and retain only the most valuable tokens within the KV cache. Representative methods include Sliding Window Attention ( Beltagy e" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/2503_05096_rag__chunk_004> a kg:Chunk ;
    kg:chunkId "2503.05096_rag::chunk_004" ;
    kg:docId "2503.05096_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2503_05096_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "2,2 Figure 2: A single-step speculative decoding process with a speculative length of 1. We primarily discuss the greedy sampling, where the token with the highest confidence score is selected as the output instead of the whole distribution. The speculative length, by controlling the number of candidate tokens generated by the draft model, directly impacts both the latency benefits and resource consumption of speculative decoding. Mainstream methods [ 5 , 20 , 21 , 30 , 38 ] rely on offline anal" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/2503_05096_rag__chunk_005> a kg:Chunk ;
    kg:chunkId "2503.05096_rag::chunk_005" ;
    kg:docId "2503.05096_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2503_05096_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "1), excessively short speculative lengths fail to fully utilize idle computational resources, leaving the acceleration potential of speculative decoding untapped. Workload characteristics represent another critical variable. We demonstrate this by analyzing workloads extracted from RAG [ 16 ], mathematical reasoning [ 8 ], and question-answering [ 18 ] datasets, each exhibiting different optimal speculative lengths. Evidently, applying the same speculative length across different requests result" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/2503_06433_rag__chunk_006> a kg:Chunk ;
    kg:chunkId "2503.06433_rag::chunk_006" ;
    kg:docId "2503.06433_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2503_06433_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "all-reduce operations but further limits the communication bandwidth, resulting in escalated communication overhead. This issue is particularly pronounced in the prefill stage, where a large number of tokens are processed simultaneously, making communication overhead the primary bottleneck. Thus, tensor parallelism tends to perform worse than pipeline parallelism due to its large communication overhead. 3 M OTIVATION AND A NALYSIS In this section, we provide an in-depth analysis of two key obser" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/2503_18292_rag__chunk_009> a kg:Chunk ;
    kg:chunkId "2503.18292_rag::chunk_009" ;
