        "2509.06261_rag::chunk_003"^^xsd:string,
        "2510.02758_rag::chunk_013"^^xsd:string ;
    :hasEvidenceText "Caching enables reusing KV cache from previous requests, avoiding redundant computation for repeated context"^^xsd:string,
        "KV cache [ 27 , 49 ] was introduced as a key mechanism to reduce inference latency: it stores intermediate results from previously generated tokens to avoid recomputing tensor values."^^xsd:string,
        "LLM engines would discard the KV cache when the user session becomes inactive to free up HBM space for other active sessions and re-compute the whole KV cache again"^^xsd:string,
        "The KV cache, while essential for transformer-based LLM and VLM family, demands significant computational resources and memory, limiting inference speed."^^xsd:string,
        "The generated K pre and V pre are stored in the KV cache."^^xsd:string,
        "They maintain a KV cache that stores keyvalue pairs for all previously processed tokens at each layer."^^xsd:string,
        "TokenFlow exploits GPU I/O idle periods to preemptively offload KV caches to CPU memory."^^xsd:string,
        "generates the key and value cache (KV cache) for future decoding"^^xsd:string,
        "intermediate state, specifically the key-value (K,V) caches, from previous requests in the ongoing interaction."^^xsd:string,
        "migrates each request by transferring either tokens or KV cache"^^xsd:string,
        "the Key-Value cache ( KV cache ) acts as a major performance bottleneck in LLM serving."^^xsd:string,
        "the computed Key and Value tensors are stored in the GPU memory as a Key-Value Cache (KV Cache) to alleviate computational overhead in subsequent operations."^^xsd:string,
        "the model utilizes the entire sequence of keys and values from time steps 1 to t (stored in the KV cache) alongside the new query Q t"^^xsd:string,
        "the prompt KV cache is transferred from the prompt processing to the token generation machines."^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:subClassOf :memory,
        owl:Thing ;
    skos:altLabel "KV cache"^^xsd:string,
        "KV-Cache"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:skos_definition "A mechanism that stores intermediate results from previously generated tokens to avoid recomputing tensor values, essential for enhancing inference speed."^^xsd:string ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom "CQ_S0_R1_0001"^^xsd:string,
        "CQ_S0_R1_0011"^^xsd:string,
