    kg:docId "2512.03416_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2512_03416_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "TokenScale: Timely and Accurate Autoscaling for Disaggregated LLM Serving with Token Velocity Ruiqi Lai Hongrui Liu Siyu Cao * Chengzhi Lu NTU Singapore Singapore chengzhi.lu@ntu.edu.sg Zonghao Liu NTU Singapore Singapore liuz0138@e.ntu.edu.sg NTU Singapore Singapore ruiqi003@e.ntu.edu.sg NTU Singapore Singapore hongrui001@e.ntu.edu.sg NTU Singapore Singapore scao010@e.ntu.edu.sg Siyang Shao * Yixin Zhang * Luo Mai University of Edinburgh Edinburgh, UK lmai@ed.ac.uk Dmitrii Ustiugov NTU Singapor" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/2512_03416_rag__chunk_002> a kg:Chunk ;
    kg:chunkId "2512.03416_rag::chunk_002" ;
    kg:docId "2512.03416_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2512_03416_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "have spare compute cycles. When a burst arrives, excessive prefill requests are routed to the Convertible Decoders. To prevent resource contention with ongoing decoding tasks, we use an SLO-aware restricted chunked-prefill strategy. This involves carefully sizing prefill chunks and reserving a dedicated portion of GPU memory and compute, ensuring that neither the co-located decoding tasks nor the new prefill tasks violate their TTFT or TPOT SLOs. After processing the prefill chunks, the instance" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/5431dca75a8d2abc1fb51e89e8324f10-Paper-Conference_rag__chunk_004> a kg:Chunk ;
    kg:chunkId "5431dca75a8d2abc1fb51e89e8324f10-Paper-Conference_rag::chunk_004" ;
    kg:docId "5431dca75a8d2abc1fb51e89e8324f10-Paper-Conference_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/5431dca75a8d2abc1fb51e89e8324f10-Paper-Conference_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "parallelism strategy that aligns with our purpose. Furthermore, section 3.2 investigates the guidelines for the distribution of computations to enable effective overlap among the CPU, GPU, and I/O under such parallelism strategy. In the context of pipeline parallelism, the model is segmented into distinct parts, and computations are executed sequentially on various devices. As evident from the illustration, in order to maximize utilization, it is crucial to ensure that the CPU computation time f" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/906419cd502575b617cc489a1a696a67-Paper-Conference_rag__chunk_001> a kg:Chunk ;
    kg:chunkId "906419cd502575b617cc489a1a696a67-Paper-Conference_rag::chunk_001" ;
    kg:docId "906419cd502575b617cc489a1a696a67-Paper-Conference_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/906419cd502575b617cc489a1a696a67-Paper-Conference_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "of the key innovations in the LoRA paper was the elimination of adapter inference latency by directly merging the adapter with the model parameters. Additionally, to support multiple models on a single machine, the same paper proposes swapping adapters by adding and subtracting LoRA weights from the base model. While this approach enables low-latency inference for a single adapter and serial execution across adapters, it significantly reduces overall serving throughput and increases total latenc" .

